WEBVTT

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:08.110
Wulaosu!
Thunder Punch!

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.080
Infight!

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.800
This will finish it!

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.800
Oh! Here it is!
A Trial Mission!

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.260
What’s this one like?

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.390
“Choose one of the following two”...

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:35.850
One is...
“Follow the three Sacred Footprints.”

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.350
The other one is...
“Catch Regieleki/Regidrago.”

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.650
Both sound awesome.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:44.650
“Additionally,
this will be the last mission.”

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.320
Huh?

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.670
The final Trial Mission
for Project Mew has finally arrived.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:34.680
Those who clear it
will be awarded three tokens,

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.680
and the three with the highest totals
will be accepted.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.850
Currently first is Shigeru,
with 12.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:43.270
Second: Layla, with 9.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:46.690
Four people are in third with 8,
including Tokio and Shun'ya.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.940
Go, with 7, is seventh.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:55.030
Even if I clear this mission,
it all depends on the other Challengers’ results.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.570
For now,
you just gotta do all you can.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:58.950
Yeah!

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.200
So what’re you gonna pick?

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.700
All right, this one!

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.210
“Catch Regieleki/Regidrago.”

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.840
I’ve heard of Regice and Regirock,
but those...

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.460
These are Pokémon
we don’t have much data on yet.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.090
If it’s called Regieleki,
is it an Electric type?

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.890
And Regidrago sounds like
a Dragon-type, right?

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:23.930
Apparently they’re somehow connected
with the Ruins of Decision in Galar’s Crown Snowfield.

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.730
The Ruins of Decision...

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:28.230
This is getting me pumped up!

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.980
Let’s get going, Go!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.980
No. I’m going alone this time.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.740
Huh?! How come?

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.360
I’m going to work hard
at my own goals.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.740
So Satoshi,
I want you working hard at yours.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.700
Go...

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.000
Got it.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.620
I’ll go train for
the Masters Tournament.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.830
So make sure
you clear the mission, Go!

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.130
Right!

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.850
The future lies in my hands...

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:07.640
Let’s do this!
Project Mew, last mission!

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:19.700
And if I pass through here...

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:23.580
The Ruins of Decision!

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.580
Huh?

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.880
Shigeru?

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.960
You took your time, Go.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.170
You were waiting?
For me?

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.470
Would I do that?

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.840
Don’t you think
these ruins are strange?

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:41.970
Yeah.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.470
The colors being split like this...

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.730
Hmm.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.060
Go. There’s ancient symbols.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.270
Huh?!

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.360
Oh...

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:58.650
There’s probably
a seal on this door.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.610
I wonder what it says...

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:05.370
“A giant of rock. A giant of ice.
A giant of steel”...

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:10.210
“When mustered are the giants three,
opened shall the door of destiny be.”

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.120
Mr. Tsurugi!

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.130
Can you tell what it means?

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:17.380
If we gather three giants,
this door will open.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.130
What are the three?

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:25.300
“Rock, ice, and steel” can only mean
Regirock, Regice, and Registeel.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:30.390
Aren’t they... Legendary Pokémon that are important
for studying the origin of Pokémon as a whole?

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.350
Precisely.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.650
Come on out!

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.150
Ooh!

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.030
You finally got them all.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.280
On top of these three,
it’s said there are two unknown giants inside.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:01.130
Go investigate.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:05.640
But from here on,
you may only use two Pokémon.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.050
Right!

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:14.810
You’ve learned a little bit
about cooperation, haven’t you?

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:15.900
Yeah.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:20.530
Still, having you battle Tokio
one-on-one at the very end...

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:22.150
Ms. Asahi has a mean streak
of her own.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:22.650
H—?

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.030
You were watching that mission?

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:29.990
Maybe I was.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:34.120
I want to confirm whether you’re worthy
of working by my side.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:38.920
Wh—?
What are you trying to say?

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.510
Why are you trying to meet Mew?

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:45.840
Remember what
Professor Hodaka said?

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.140
What are Pokémon,
and where did they come from?

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:53.810
The solution lies with Mew,
who holds the genes of all Pokémon,

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:57.190
and is thought to be
ancestor to all Pokémon.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.150
And I even met Mew
when I was young.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.110
Huh.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:05.030
I want to know
so much more about Pokémon.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:08.700
That’s why
I really want to see Mew again!

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.330
Just like me, then...

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:14.750
I think you said you were researching
everything to do with Pokémon.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:15.710
Yes.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.880
And Mew is
a necessary part of that.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:22.630
I also believe that meeting Mew will bring us closer
to solving the mysteries of Pokémon.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:25.840
Oh, how I want to meet Mew...

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.760
I’m sure you will!

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:35.230
Statues on the left and right...
Round patterns on the floor...

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:38.650
This room is pretty suspicious.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:39.560
Yeah.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.900
There must be some trick to it.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.450
Now that you mention it...

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:57.160
Maybe the patterns
at the entrance are a hint...

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.750
In which case...

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.880
If I step on the same pattern
as those...

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:05.800
Bingo!

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.430
All right...
I’m not gonna lose to you!

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:18.600
Seems like only one set of floor switches,
left or right, will light up at once...

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.520
Sorry, but I’m going first!

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:42.170
What now, Shigeru?
This is getting us nowhere...

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:45.460
How about we battle
to decide who takes priority?

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.420
Oh...
You want one?

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.420
Mm-hmm!

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:53.050
But first,
there’s one thing I’d like to try.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.640
Rather than
one or the other...

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:00.190
I’m wondering if there’s a way
for us to catch both.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:03.560
Not just one, but both...

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.570
At the same time...

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.280
I get it!

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:09.400
Collaboration
instead of obstruction!

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.990
If we sync up and step on both
at the same time...

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:12.820
Let’s give it a try.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.910
Ready, and...

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:17.870
We did it!

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.500
Just as we predicted.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.760
Next is the last one!

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:31.970
We don’t know what’ll happen
once we step on it.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:33.590
Keep your cool.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.600
Back at you!

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:37.470
Mosnow, use Icicle Spears!

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.100
Hihidaruma, use Icicle Drop!

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.530
Layla and Shun'ya?!

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:05.880
Next is the last one!

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:08.130
We don’t know what’ll happen
once we step on it.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:09.710
Keep your cool.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.220
Back at you!

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:13.630
Mosnow, use Icicle Spears!

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.260
Hihidaruma, use Icicle Drop!

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.350
Layla and Shun'ya?!

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:28.270
I owe you big time for
Sea Kinsetsu, Go.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:35.660
There’s Go, seventh
in the interim rankings...

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:38.280
...but the real prize we caught here
is the frontrunner, Shigeru!

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:42.040
So you’re going to just
steal our idea, is that it?

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.120
That’s a dirty trick!

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.170
Well, we’re Challengers.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:48.290
We’ll do whatever
it takes to win.

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:50.130
Correct.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:54.050
Which is why I had to come prepared
for any and all complications.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:55.180
Me, too!

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:57.180
Brimuon! Psycho Cutter!

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:59.220
Aceburn, use Blaze Kick!

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.770
Shigeru, let’s work together!

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:08.060
I’ve been waiting for you
to say that!

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:11.360
So we’re settling it
with a tag battle?

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:12.530
Yes.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.070
Considering
we’ll need them for later,

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.200
we should limit our Pokémon usage
as much as possible.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:22.700
What would you say to one Pokémon each,
with no Pokémon change-outs?

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.580
Sure.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.370
I don’t see any reason to refuse.

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:30.750
Sadaija and Deathban, huh?

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:33.630
I expected Go
to use his Aceburn...

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:37.590
...but I didn’t expect
Shigeru to bring out Kamex.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:42.350
I predicted you’d pick Rock or Ground types,
which have an advantage over Fire types,

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:45.230
so I chose a Water type
to counter that.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:48.690
I can see why you’re
provisionally ranked first.

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.820
But we didn’t come here
just to lose!

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:53.400
Use Sand Hell on Aceburn!

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.160
Aceburn!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.200
Blow it away
with Hydro Pump!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.160
Shigeru...

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.710
You can thank me later!

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:10.210
They’re about to attack again!

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:11.210
Ground Stomp!

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:16.720
Go! Get on Kamex!

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:19.970
Aceburn,
ride on Kamex’s back!

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.930
Shoot a Water Pulse
at the ground!

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:24.930
Our Ground Stomp...

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:25.930
They dodged it!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.100
Now, Go!

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.690
Blaze Kick!

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.410
N-Next!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:45.540
Give it up.

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:46.540
Layla!

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:48.290
A promise is a promise.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:51.290
If you won’t keep your promise,
<i>I’ll</i> take you on.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.460
What sportsmanship.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:56.130
But that’s not all, is it?

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:56.960
Hmph.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.050
You saw right through me, huh?

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:02.220
If we fail at catching
Regidrago and Regieleki,

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:04.560
it becomes your turn to try.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:09.230
Of course, Regidrago and Regieleki
will be weakened after our battle!

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:12.900
Which will make our battle
all the easier.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:15.860
Amazing, Layla!
You’re so sneaky!

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:18.570
Don’t get your hopes up
while you wait.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:57.900
Discharge?!

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.740
So this one’s Regieleki?

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:02.450
Then this is Regidrago!

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:05.530
You handle Regieleki!

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:06.950
Got it.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.370
Flygon, go!

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:08.370
Brimuon!

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.000
Don’t let your guard down!

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.380
Back at you!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.130
It’s fast...
Hit it back with Mud Shot!

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:27.720
What is that move?!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.470
Block it with Magical Shine!

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:41.780
An electrical cage?

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:43.740
Go!

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:48.120
Dragon Breath!

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:54.920
Brimuon!

00:14:58.670 --> 00:14:59.420
Divine Speed?!

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:00.170
Here it comes!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.050
Arm Hammer!

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:05.930
Flygon!

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:05.930
Brimuon!

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:12.810
You did your best, Flygon.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:15.810
Take a good rest, Brimuon.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.360
They’re working as a team.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.610
Yeah.
Well, bring it on!

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:23.320
Let’s go!

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:25.860
Aceburn, go!

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.660
Kamex, you too!

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.160
Use Pyro Ball on Regieleki!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.540
Use Rocket Headbutt
on Regidrago!

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:51.680
Gah...

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.810
Are they trying
to take us both down at once?!

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:56.440
Shigeru!
Use the Twister!

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:00.110
Go! Do it like you did
to dodge our Ground Stomp!

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:02.320
Thanks for the advice!

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:04.230
Kamex, use Rapid Spin!

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:06.200
Aceburn, get on Kamex!

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.950
Then use the Twister
to gain height!

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:15.910
<i>All right!</i>

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.420
Now!
Use Blaze Kick on Regieleki!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.420
Charge in with Rapid Spin!

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:43.770
Come on, Monster Ball!

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:44.400
Monster Ball, go!

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:58.290
Regidrago’s data will be
added to the Index.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:03.170
Regieleki’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:11.430
Aww, we lose.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:14.680
We never got to play a part.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:18.520
No, thank you for the advice.
It saved us.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:23.860
Go. Without your help,
I would never have caught it.

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:25.770
It’s teamwork
that gave us victory.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:26.940
Shigeru...

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:32.320
If you team up with someone unskilled
simply out of friendship, they’ll only let you down.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.450
But even if you’re rivals
with someone...

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.330
...if your goals align,
you can still work together.

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:41.540
Stubbornly clinging to your pride
will only slow you down.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.000
Acting alone
can prove fatal.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:48.130
That’s something I learned
from Mr. Tsurugi on a mission.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:51.720
You’re disqualified.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.890
Were it not for me,
you’d be dead.

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:57.680
Both you <i>and</i> your Pokémon.

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.980
So you did...
the same thing?

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:06.110
Yeah.
I nearly got myself disqualified.

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:09.280
But that experience
helped me grow.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:11.110
Is that so...?

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:15.370
So that’s why
you kept goading me...

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:16.200
No.

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:19.700
Everything I did
was for my own sake.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:29.920
Ms. Asahi?

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:32.630
So the other mission
is over, then.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:33.760
Well, yeah.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:44.190
Oh?
You caught both of them?

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:46.810
So these are
Regidrago and Regieleki.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:49.150
The legendary quintet is complete.

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:51.360
What a glorious sight...

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:07.580
Oh...!

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:14.930
A pillar... of light?

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:27.810
Regigigas...

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:29.940
And...

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:32.530
...it’s Daimaxed!

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:39.410
Did Regidrago
and the others call it here?

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:05.270
What... <i>was</i> that?

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:09.650
<i>Incoming call from Professor Hodaka!
Incoming call from Professor Hodaka!</i>

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:14.940
Now, all of the
Trial Missions are over.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.530
As the head of Project Mew,

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:20.240
I thank all the Challengers
who participated.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.740
I hope you make use
of what you learned in these missions...

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:26.960
...and keep pursuing
the mysteries of Pokémon.

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.670
Now, I will announce the results.

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:33.250
As you know,
the top three will be accepted.

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:37.470
First place is Shigeru
with 15 tokens.

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:42.010
Second place is Tokio
with 11.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:43.560
Tokio...!

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:47.270
And finally,
third place is...

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:51.650
Incoming call from Go.
Incoming call from Go.

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:53.900
Go, how’d the mission go?

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:57.190
Satoshi, I...

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.400
...passed!

00:20:58.780 --> 00:21:00.740
Really?!
Congrats, Go!

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:02.450
It’s all because of you!

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:03.990
It’s ‘cause of your hard work!

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:06.240
Thanks so much!

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.540
Okay, I’ll see you later!

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:13.040
You’re merely standing
at the starting line.

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:18.090
So let’s both do our best, Go.

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:20.430
Shigeru...

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:21.590
Yeah!

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:33.400
Alongside Shigeru and Tokio,
Go was accepted,

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:36.690
and has finally
become a Chaser.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:41.450
What sort of adventures will Project Mew
have in store for him?!

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:09.620
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.910
Go!

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:13.460
The Masters Tournament
is almost here!

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:16.250
You guys, let’s get all fired up
and get training!

00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:17.880
You’re hopeless.

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:20.420
Show some attention
for your partners’ condition!

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:21.590
Shinji!

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:25.510
That guy has a scary look in his eyes!

00:23:25.510 --> 00:23:27.640
3v3 with no switching!

00:23:27.640 --> 00:23:29.600
Stand by for battle!

00:23:29.600 --> 00:23:31.390
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:34.600
A Fire Training Battle!
Satoshi VS Shinji!!
